// Title: Suspicious File Downloaded From Direct IP Via Certutil.EXE
// ID: 13e6fe51-d478-4c7e-b0f2-6da9b400a829
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-15
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027, attack.command-and-control, attack.t1105
// Description: Detects the execution of certutil with certain flags that allow the utility to download files from direct IPs.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((((process.command_line like "*_urlcache *" or process.command_line like "*_verifyctl *" or process.command_line like "*_URL *")) and ((process.command_line like "*_://1*" or process.command_line like "*_://2*" or process.command_line like "*_://3*" or process.command_line like "*_://4*" or process.command_line like "*_://5*" or process.command_line like "*_://6*" or process.command_line like "*_://7*" or process.command_line like "*_://8*" or process.command_line like "*_://9*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\certutil.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "CertUtil.exe"))) and not ((process.command_line like "*_://7-*")))
